show and the fbi joining forces in the  search for two people accused in a  violent case out of the south valley  thank you for joining us at four i'm  kirsten joyce and i'm christian casadas  the two agencies working side by side to  find michael overton and christine  schultz investigators say they are  wanted in a murder robbery investigation  we believe the motive is that the  boyfriend had expensive jewelry that was  inside the house a mantune is on for  this couple michael overton and  christine schultz investigators  connecting them to that murder robbery  on march 25 at a home on bright nimbus  avenue near robindale and jones when  units arrived on scene they located a  deceased 24 year old woman suffering  from numerous gunshot wounds the victim  natalie mandalay came face to face with  the armed intruders they got into a  shootout after the gunfire exchange one  of the males named kamari oliver  panicked and fled the residence komari  got into a white mercedes and drove off  and left the others at the scene  according to police mondelez boyfriend  arrived to the home at the same time he  chased the mercedes ramming it with his  car into a brick wall kamari took off on  foot but was arrested days later overton  schultz and another man ran from the  home we do believe there's a very high  chance that they have fled the state  we did have some information that they  had fled to the east coast but we don't  know if that's accurate while  investigators say this was a targeted  robbery they say schultz knew the victim  and orchestrated the crime the third man  has not been identified we would like  the community work with us to bring them  to justice  the fbi is offering a 20 thousand dollar  reward for the capture of the couple now  if you have any information about them  you're asked to please call the number  right there on your screen 1-800 call  fbi
 

